# domains.conf — put one domain on each line. The tool ignores an empty line
# and a line that starts with #.
#
#   cp domains.conf.example domains.conf
#
# The .gitignore file holds domains.conf. The list of your domains is data that
# you possibly do not want to make public.

example.com
example.net

# You can put a subdomain here if you own the zone. But the apex domain is
# usually correct. The tool finds the subdomains itself with Certificate
# Transparency.
